{"id":"eye","name":"Eye","aliases":["Eye"],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:eye","torrey:eye-the"],"groups":["Figurative"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Eye","text":"(Heb. ‘ain, meaning “flowing”), applied (1) to a fountain, frequently; (2) to colour (Num. 11:7; R.V., “appearance,” marg. “eye”); (3) the face (Ex. 10:5, 15; Num. 22:5, 11), in Num. 14:14, “face to face” (R.V. marg., “eye to eye”). “Between the eyes”, i.e., the forehead (Ex. 13:9, 16). The expression (Prov. 23:31), “when it giveth his colour in the cup,” is literally, “when it giveth out [or showeth] its eye.” The beads or bubbles of wine are thus spoken of. “To set the eyes” on any one is to view him with favour (Gen. 44:21; Job 24:23; Jer. 39:12). This word is used figuratively in the expressions an “evil eye” (Matt. 20:15), a “bountiful eye” (Prov. 22:9), “haughty eyes” (6:17 marg.), “wanton eyes” (Isa. 3:16), “eyes full of adultery” (2 Pet. 2:14), “the lust of the eyes” (1 John 2:16). Christians are warned against “eye-service” (Eph. 6:6; Col. 3:22). Men were sometimes punished by …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G3788","lemma":"ὀφθαλμός","xlit":"ophthalmós","gloss":"the eye","kjv":"eye, sight","count":9,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H5027","lemma":"נָבַט","xlit":"nâbaṭ","gloss":"to scan","kjv":"behold, consider, look, regard","count":4,"share":0.06},{"strong":"G3650","lemma":"ὅλος","xlit":"hólos","gloss":"\"whole\" or \"all\"","kjv":"all, altogether, every whit, + throughout","count":4,"share":0.06},{"strong":"G4675","lemma":"σοῦ","xlit":"soû","gloss":"of thee, thy","kjv":"X home, thee, thine, thou","count":5,"share":0.07},{"strong":"G4983","lemma":"σῶμα","xlit":"sōma","gloss":"the body , used in a very wide application, literally or","kjv":"bodily, body, slave","count":4,"share":0.06},{"strong":"H3708","lemma":"כַּעַס","xlit":"kaʻaç","gloss":"vexation","kjv":"anger, angry, grief, indignation","count":3,"share":0.04}],"verses":["Matt.5.29","Matt.5.38","Matt.6.22","Matt.6.23","Luke